      "claim": "Quire Boundary Lexical Discontinuity Law (z = +5.21)",
      "verdict": "TRIVIAL-OR-CONFOUNDED",
      "key_audit_finding": "11 of 17 cross-quire steps also change section ($I), language ($L), or hand ($H), and the remaining 6 occur only in short-text Herbal-A (4) and Zodiac (2) folios (whereas long-text Balneological $I=B and Starred Recipes $I=S have 42 within-quire steps and 0 pure cross-quire steps). Within the matched H/A/1 + Z/?/4 cohorts, canonical Jaccard is 0.1258 vs 0.0987 (z=+1.73, p=0.080). In multiple OLS regression controlling for ($I,$L,$H) and folio word count (R^2=0.594), quire_change is non-significant: coef=-0.0160 (t=-1.82, p=0.072)."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": 2,
      "discovery": "Discovery 251 (Attack 234)",
      "claim": "Recto-to-Verso Spatial Registration Law (z = -4.60) & 1.4-3.5 mm unpainted reserve border",
      "verdict": "TRIVIAL-OR-CONFOUNDED (registration) / UNSUPPORTED (universal reserve border)",
